### Advantages

* Simple
* Easy to understand
* Good separation of concerns
* Suitable for CRUD/business applications

### Problems

* Layers can become tightly coupled
* Business logic can leak into controllers/repositories
* Difficult to scale individual components independently

### Use when

* Enterprise CRUD applications
* Moderate complexity
* Traditional business systems

### Architect-level point

Don't confuse **logical layers** with **physical deployment tiers**.

You can have a layered architecture deployed as a single monolith.

