# 5. SOA — Service-Oriented Architecture

SOA also decomposes systems into services, but traditionally services tend to be **larger enterprise capabilities** and often use centralized infrastructure.

```text
              Enterprise Service Bus
                       │
       ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐
       ↓               ↓               ↓
 Customer Service   Order Service   Billing
```

### Microservices vs SOA

| SOA                          | Microservices                |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Larger services              | Smaller bounded services     |
| Often centralized ESB        | Usually decentralized        |
| Enterprise integration focus | Autonomous deployment        |
| Shared infrastructure common | Service ownership emphasized |
| Governance-heavy             | Team autonomy                |

