# 13. Saga Pattern

Used for **distributed transactions**.

Suppose:

```text
Order
 ↓
Payment
 ↓
Inventory
 ↓
Shipping
```

There is no single database transaction across all services.

Saga manages the distributed workflow.

Two major approaches:

### Choreography

Services react to events.

```text
OrderCreated
     ↓
PaymentCompleted
     ↓
InventoryReserved
     ↓
OrderConfirmed
```

### Orchestration

Central orchestrator controls workflow.

```text
           Saga Orchestrator
           /       |       \
          ↓        ↓        ↓
       Order    Payment  Inventory
```

### Architect interview point

Saga requires **compensating actions**.

Example:

```text
Payment successful
Inventory failed

→ Refund payment
```

