# 15. API Gateway Pattern

Client doesn't communicate directly with every microservice.

```text
              Client
                 │
                 ↓
             API Gateway
          /      |       \
         ↓       ↓        ↓
      Orders  Payment  Customer
```

Responsibilities may include:

* Routing
* Authentication
* Authorization
* Rate limiting
* Request aggregation
* TLS termination
* API versioning

Examples:

* Azure API Management
* Kong
* AWS API Gateway

---

# 16. Backend for Frontend — BFF

Useful when different clients have different requirements.

```text
             Clients
          /     |     \
         ↓      ↓      ↓
      Mobile   Web   Partner
         ↓      ↓      ↓
       BFF    BFF    BFF
         \      |      /
          Microservices
```

For example:

```text
Mobile BFF → lightweight response
Web BFF    → detailed response
```

Instead of forcing every client to consume the same API shape.

---

# 17. Client-Server Architecture

Classic distributed architecture:

```text
Client
   ↓
Server
   ↓
Database
```

Examples:

* Web applications
* Desktop applications
* Mobile applications

It's one of the foundational architectural styles.

---

# 18. Peer-to-Peer Architecture

There is no single central server.

```text
Node A ───── Node B
  │           │
  │           │
Node C ───── Node D
```

Examples historically include:

* File sharing
* Blockchain networks
* Distributed systems

