# 20. Pipe-and-Filter Architecture

Data passes through a sequence of processing stages.

```text
Input
  ↓
Filter 1
  ↓
Filter 2
  ↓
Filter 3
  ↓
Output
```

Example:

```text
Read File
   ↓
Parse
   ↓
Validate
   ↓
Transform
   ↓
Store
```

Common in:

* Data processing
* ETL
* Compilers
* Streaming pipelines

---

# 21. Space-Based Architecture

Designed for extreme scalability.

Instead of depending heavily on a central database:

```text
       Load Balancer
       /           \
      ↓             ↓
 Processing Unit  Processing Unit
      ↓             ↓
   In-memory Data Grid
```

Useful for:

* High-volume transaction systems
* Very high scalability
* Low-latency applications

---

# 22. Broker Architecture

A broker mediates communication between components.

```text
Producer
   ↓
 Broker
   ↓
Consumer
```

Examples:

```text
Kafka
RabbitMQ
Azure Service Bus
```

The broker provides decoupling between producers and consumers.

---

# 23. Microkernel / Plugin Architecture

Core system + plugins.

```text
             Core
          /    |    \
         ↓     ↓     ↓
     Plugin  Plugin Plugin
       A       B      C
```

Examples:

* IDEs
* Browsers
* Product platforms
* Extensible enterprise systems

Useful when functionality needs to be added without changing the core.

